{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1012287-swarm-form","id":1012287,"title":"Swarm form","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-04T17:42:09-08:00","id":1012287,"title":"Swarm form","content":"To attack those within her swarm, roll Strength + Brawl, ignoring Defense. Divide the damage however you wish among those inside. Apply a victim\u2019s armor to the damage normally. The damage is lethal (bashing to Kindred). Alternately, a success may instead allow the vampire to take one Vitae from a victim.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does this mean that the attacking swarm of bats uses its bat strength or its normal strength? Can you use your protean claws in swarm form?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T01:43:58-08:00","id":1012449,"title":"","content":"The vampire's own Strength + Brawl. I'd say you can activate Predatory/Unnatural Aspects in Swarm Form as you can with Beast Skin as is a variant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:44:40-08:00","id":1012698,"title":"","content":"beast's skin says that you use the physicals of the animal you have taken. So I would say that you use your bat's attack pool. But that's just my take on it. <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;In animal form, she takes on the beast\u2019s Physical Attributes<br /> and Skills, and its Size, Speed, and Health&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:58:26-08:00","id":1012706,"title":"","content":"I just use the Swarm Tilt from Demon. It's much cleaner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T12:51:42-08:00","id":1012730,"title":"","content":"Are you allowed to reproduce the text of that Tilt for those of us that haven't purchased Demon yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:07:52-08:00","id":1012768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1012287-swarm-form?p=1012730#post1012730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you allowed to reproduce the text of that Tilt for those of us that haven't purchased Demon yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Swarm (Environmental)</u><br /> Animals of Size 1 are generally best represented by swarms, ocks and other groupings of the animals. Swarms are measured by their radius in yards. A swarm inflicts one point of bashing damage to anyone within its radius. A swarm can inflit more damage by condensing. Every time the swarm condenses to cover half of its full area, it inflictd one additional point of damage per turn.<br /> Therefore, a swarm of eight yards in radius inflicts two bashing damage per turn if it constricts down to a four- yard radius, three bashing if it halves that again to a two-yard radius, and four bashing damage per turn it if condensed itself down to a one-yard radius. Though condensing doesn\u2019t usually happen all that often in nature (save in the case of creatures such as killer bees), it is an easy enough thing for a being with supernatural powers to command them to do so.<br /> Armor is effective against a swarm only if it covers one\u2019s full body, but even then it provides only half its rating. In addition, targets are distracted by the swarm, suffering \u20132 dice on all rolls while they are within the radius, even if they\u2019re not specifically attacked.<br /> Causing the Tilt: The Swarm Exploit can cause this Tilt, as can similar powers from non-demonic sources. The Tilt can occur naturally if someone disturbs a nest of bees.<br /> Ending the Tilt: The swarm cannot be attacked with fists, clubs, swords or guns. Only area-effect attacks such as a torch affect it. Each point of damage inflicted by a flame or other applicable attack halves the swarm\u2019s size. Once the swarm is reduced below a one-yard radius, either all insects are dead or the few remaining disperse. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:06:10-08:00","id":1013344,"title":"","content":"I read it to mean that you use the Vampires strength. Yeah a bat might only have 1 STR but how many are in that swarm? A dozen, a few dozen? It's obviously not 12 STR but it's more than 1 unless you want to roll 12+ attacks with 1 STR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 12-06-2016, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:08:03-08:00","id":1013370,"title":"","content":"The Swarm Form ability use the vampire's Strength + Brawl for attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:07:09-08:00","id":1013731,"title":"","content":"<br /> The vampire could potentially have a ton more strength than a tiger, but when they turn into a tiger with Beast's skin, which swarm form is Beast's skin, they still have to use the tiger's strength and brawl. Swarm form says &quot;While using beast's skin&quot; and beast's skin says &quot;use the animal's stats.. ect&quot; Why would swarm form be the exception and use the vampire's stats?<br /> I am not saying your take on using the vampire's stats is wrong. I am just asking for how you got there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But as charlaquin said, using the swarm tilt from demon solves all that. :<br /> <br /> <i>Therefore, a swarm of eight yards in radius inflicts two bashing damage per turn if it constricts down to a four- yard radius, three bashing if it halves that again to a two-yard radius, and four bashing damage per turn it if condensed itself down to a one-yard radius. Though condensing doesn\u2019t usually happen all that often in nature (save in the case of creatures such as killer bees), it is an easy enough thing for a being with supernatural powers to command them to do so.</i><br /> <br /> \u200bI like this explanation of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-07-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:42:08-08:00","id":1013754,"title":"","content":"Using one animal's stats means you're attacking with one animal. That's explicitly not the case with Swarm Form where you can deal damage to multiple targets.<br /> While the rules doesn't say so (and RAW actually is using the animal's stats) it makes more sense using the vampire's own stats since animals of Size 1 have atrocious dice pools and animals of Size 0 might even be reduced to a chance die (if it weren't for Vigor). The largest of the four paragraphs describing the Merit relates to combat so I believe the Merit is supposed to be viable in combat. This would not be the case unless the user has both Protean 3 and decent Vigor, two disciplines that doesn't share a clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-07-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:09:46-08:00","id":1013770,"title":"","content":"Vampires normal stats. Swarm Form *replaces* the discipline's normal effect. It doesnt modify it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:20:08-08:00","id":1013776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1012287-swarm-form?p=1013770#post1013770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires normal stats. Swarm Form *replaces* the discipline's normal effect. It doesnt modify it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually it doesnt replace it, it does modify it by giving you a swarm form. It literally says while using the discipline.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot; When taking the <b>Beast\u2019s Skin, some Gangrel can instead become a swarm of small creatures</b>: Size 0 or Size 1 animals. &quot; </i> So instead of 1 predatory animal, it can now be a swarm But it still says while using the discipline.<br /> <br /> Edit: however, if it really does replace the discipline and you are using something completely different, that would mean you do not have to spend the 2 vitae to change shapes.<br /> Edit again,..: And that you dont get additional animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-07-2016, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T10:37:11-08:00","id":1013832,"title":"","content":"And this is why I prefer to just use the Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T11:12:34-08:00","id":1013852,"title":"","content":"As written it does use the animal's strength, so as written you roll (30 or 60sh?) bat attacks with the bat's STR and the vampires Brawl, some of which will certainly explode with 10's.<br /> Both Charlaquin's way and using the vampires STR are shortcuts to avoid that mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 12-07-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:06:31-08:00","id":1013932,"title":"","content":"You do not roll for each individual creature in the swarm. Nothing in the rules says that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T14:21:44-08:00","id":1013978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1012287-swarm-form?p=1013932#post1013932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not roll for each individual creature in the swarm. Nothing in the rules says that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Rathamus is getting at is that if you take &quot;When taking the Beast\u2019s Skin, some Gangrel can instead become a swarm of small creatures: Size 0 or Size 1 animals&quot; as meaning that you use the form's stats for rolls, you would also need to consider the fact that the form is not one animal but dozens, possibly hundreds. In theory, each bat or whatever would have a bat's strength and brawl, but they all attack as a single combatant, so it doesn't really make sense to roll a single bat's strength + brawl for an attack being made by dozens of bats simultaneously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T11:14:51-07:00","id":1063940,"title":"","content":"What nobody seems to have mentioned here yet is that there <i>are</i> rules for a Swarm of Vermin, published in the Chronicles of Darkness main book.<br /> <br /> The Trained Guard Dog profile (p.121) &quot;Doubles as: K-9 hound, wild animal, <b>swarm of vermin</b>, genetic experiment.&quot;<br /> <br /> So the Vampire's attack dice in Swarm Form should be 6, in the same way that if they become a cat their attack pool drops to 3 or if they become a Badger it becomes 5.<br /> <br /> 6 dice to attack, ignoring defence, while gaining the massive defensive benefits of Swarm Form still makes it a bargain - especially as other disciplines can be used at the same time to further boost the damage and resilience.<br /> <br /> The uncertainty makes sense if there aren't rules for a swarm that involve rolling its Strength + Brawl to attack...but there are.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13062-aetou","name":"Aetou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}